if(i)return A.bB(B.J,B.f,f,B.D,"Psyllium husk is composed predominantly of highly branched arabinoxylan polymers (arabinose and xylose monosaccharide units). The dense presence of hydroxyl (-OH) groups allows psyllium to form hydrogen bonds with surrounding water molecules, swelling up to 10\u201314 times its original volume.\n\nBecause the human small intestine lacks endogenous enzymes capable of cleaving these complex beta-linkages, the viscous gel passes intact into the colon. In the colon, it normalizes stool moisture (softening hard stool in constipation, binding excess water in diarrhea) and undergoes slow, non-gas-producing bacterial fermentation that generates beneficial short-chain fatty acids (acetate, propionate, butyrate).",B.O,B.RP,g,g,B.cx,"Biological Mechanism of Psyllium (Isabgol)",g,g,g,B.Yl,g,e,a1,"The hydrophilic polysaccharide structure is what drives its therapeutic efficacy.","MECH-"+Date.now(),B.bF,"Physiological mechanism summary based on peer-reviewed gastroenterological literature.",g,g)
